          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.035,
            0.584,
            0.099
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Garbage In, Garbage Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.23,
            0.815,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "“On\ttwo\toccasions I\thave\tbeen\tasked\t[by members\tof\tParliament],\t‘Pray,\tMr.\tBabbage, if\tyou\tput\tinto\tthe\tmachine\twrong\tfigures, will\tthe\tright\tanswers\tcome\tout?’\tI\tam\tnot able\trightly\tto\tapprehend\tthe\tkind\tof confusion\tof\tideas\tthat\tcould\tprovoke\tsuch a question.” – Charles\tBabbage\t(1791-1871)"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.968,
            0.55,
            0.986
          ],
          "content": "6.0002\tLECTURE 14"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.893,
            0.965,
            0.911,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "19"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 19,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.035,
            0.807,
            0.097
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Calhoun’s\tR esponse\tt o\tErrors\ti n \tData"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.043,
            0.202,
            0.946,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "“there were so many errors they balanced one another,\tand led to the same conclusion as if they were all correct.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.043,
            0.323,
            0.898,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "Was it the case that the measurement errors are unbiased and independent of each of other,\tand therefore almost identically distributed on either\tside of the mean?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.044,
            0.493,
            0.898,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "No,\tlater\tanalysis showed that the errors were not random but systematic."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.044,
            0.615,
            0.939,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "“it\twas the census that\twas insane and not\tthe colored people.”— James Freeman Clarke"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.044,
            0.737,
            0.918,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": "**Moral:\tAnalysis of bad\tdata can\tlead\tto dangerous conclusions.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.967,
            0.551,
            0.987
          ],
          "content": "6.0002\tLECTURE 14"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.891,
            0.968,
            0.912,
            0.989
          ],
          "content": "20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.035,
            0.279,
            0.1
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Sampling"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.174,
            0.885,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "§All\tstatistical\ttechniques\tare\tbased\tupon\tthe assumption\tthat\tby\tsampling a\tsubset\tof a\tpopulation we\tcan\tinfer\tthings\tabout\tthe\tpopulation\tas a\twhole"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.356,
            0.889,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "§As\twe\thave\tseen,\tif\trandom\tsampling\tis\tused,\tone\tcan make\tmeaningful\tmathematical\tstatements\tabout\tthe expected\trelation\tof\tthe\tsample\tto\tthe\tentire population"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.591,
            0.729,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": "§Easy\tto\tget\trandom\tsamples\tin\tsimulations"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.669,
            0.842,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "§Not\tso\teasy\tin\tthe\tfield,\twhere\tsome\texamples\tare more\tconvenient\tto\tacquire\tthan\tothers"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.967,
            0.55,
            0.987
          ],
          "content": "6.0002\tLECTURE 14"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.892,
            0.969,
            0.911,
            0.989
          ],
          "content": "21"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 21,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.036,
            0.666,
            0.1
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Non-representative Sampling"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.17,
            0.901,
            0.313
          ],
          "content": "§“Convenience\tsampling”\tnot\tusually\trandom,\te.g., ◦ Survivor\tbias,\te.g.,\tcourse evaluations at end of course or grading\tfinal\texam\tin 6.0002\ton a strict curve"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.32,
            0.894,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": "◦ Non-response bias,\te.g.,\topinion polls conducted by mail or\tonline"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.435,
            0.887,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": "§When\tsamples\tnot\trandom\tand\tindependent,\twe\tcan still\tdo\tthings\tlike\tcomputer\tmeans\tand\tstandard deviations,\tbut **we should\tnot draw\tconclusions\tfrom them** using\tthings\tlike\tthe\tempirical\trule\tand central limit\ttheorem."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.693,
            0.903,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": "§Moral:\tUnderstand\thow\tdata\twas\tcollected,\tand whether\tassumptions\tused\tin\tthe\tanalysis\tare\tsatisfied. If\tnot,\tbe\twary."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
